WEBVTT

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.040
You win!

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.050
Wow!  He won again!

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:30.240
It’s about 70% finished, but our virtual 
Playmaker stands no chance against him anymore.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:34.260
Lock disengaged.  Ending program.

00:00:54.310 --> 00:01:00.320
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:07.110
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:14.430
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:21.000
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:27.750
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:34.980
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:41.690
I want to share your pain

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.890
Playmaker, are you here?

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:23.540
Stop and listen.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:29.330
If you turn around, we’re 
done.  I’ll leave.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:32.340
Are you really Playmaker?

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:36.310
Security Manager Zaizen, 
you’re very distrustful.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:38.560
The Dark Ignis.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:43.550
It's unusual that you'd come to meet me.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:47.250
The Ignis are monitoring the network.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:51.020
If we travel through the 
net, they’ll detect us.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.990
Did something serious occur?

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:57.000
Hey, good instincts.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:02.730
I must tell you something 
about the two new Ignis.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:05.970
So that’s Aoi Zaizen’s brother.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:11.190
I don’t think it’s good to share 
our info with SOL Technologies.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:14.050
You’re very distrustful.

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:16.080
Didn’t SOL create you?

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:21.100
But it's now a lair of bounty 
hunters that hunt us.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.050
They can’t be trusted.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:26.060
Is what you said true, Playmaker?

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:29.030
Do you think we’d lie?

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:33.950
Sorry.  The Ignis declared 
war against humans…

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:37.840
What you said was too shocking.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:40.560
We plan to stop Lightning.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:44.610
But we don’t know how they'll attack us.

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:49.580
They may cause greater damage to 
LINK VRAINS than the Tower of Hanoi.

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:51.550
To LINK VRAINS?

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:53.770
Just in case…

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:57.550
Only you can save LINK VRAINS then.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:59.260
We’re counting on you, Zaizen.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.220
You came here to warn me.

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:06.230
Playmaker?

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.000
The Ignis are rebelling?

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:18.320
Yes.  According to Playmaker, 
the Light Ignis, Wind Ignis

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:22.210
and an AI named Bohman 
are enemies of mankind.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:25.550
The Ignis had a falling out between them?

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:28.180
It’s not that simple.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:33.090
The enemy Ignis want to 
conquer humans right away.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:35.070
Conquer humans?

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:39.960
Ironically, what the Knights 
of Hanoi said is coming true.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:42.290
But we have allies.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:47.010
Ai and Flame don’t view 
humans as the enemy.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.470
They coexist with humans.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:54.310
The enemy Ignis want to 
fight Playmaker's team.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.830
So the Ignis will defeat each other?

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:05.190
If Playmaker loses, we may face 
the worst possible outcome.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:08.190
The worst outcome...

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:11.200
I heard there were a total of six Ignis.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.000
What about the remaining two?

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.560
I don’t know where they went.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.330
They’re neutral.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:23.840
I’ll go back to work and recheck 
LINK VRAINS’s security.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:27.350
We’ll search for the two neutral Ignis.

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:32.020
If they side with the humans, 
we’ll have the numbers advantage.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:34.520
But if they join the enemy…

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.260
I don’t want to think what'll happen.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:39.440
Don’t do anything crazy.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:40.260
Right!

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:46.310
That idiot Earth!  He doesn’t 
show up when it's important!

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:51.120
Aqua went missing before 
Cyberse World was attacked.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:55.870
I don’t think those two will 
align with Lightning, but…

00:05:55.870 --> 00:06:00.850
But Lightning won’t ignore 
those who don’t obey him.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.540
We have to find them quickly!

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:06.280
They’re in danger.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:07.750
Kusanagi.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:10.450
Yeah.  It’s finally complete.

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:12.760
Find something?

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:16.420
Earth often appeared in LINK VRAINS.

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:20.060
Yusaku and I identified suspicious traces.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:23.840
Earth may be hiding somewhere among them.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:26.020
There's so many spots!

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:28.310
He's been wandering that much?

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:32.340
Knowing Earth, he may be searching for Aqua.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:33.620
Oh yeah.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.790
He does take things seriously.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.510
He'd search every blade of grass.

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:49.170
You don't see this often.  
Why's it like this?

00:06:57.910 --> 00:06:59.330
What's this?

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:02.310
Is something there?

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:10.290
Aqua!

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:13.480
You’re…

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:16.120
You came to save me?

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:18.470
I’m glad you’re okay, Aqua!

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:20.020
Aqua?

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:21.420
That’s your name.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:24.400
Call me Earth.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:25.920
Earth…

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.450
I’ll save you!

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:32.600
Don’t overdo it!  This program is-

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:35.600
I’m fine!  This is nothing!

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:44.740
Are you okay?

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:48.880
Yes.  Let’s flee!

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:54.900
Soulburner, let’s split up and search.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:57.900
Okay!  I’ll go down!

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:04.680
I see.

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:09.910
Like I thought, Cyberse World was destroyed.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:13.880
It seems you know something?

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:14.940
Yes.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:21.120
The one who locked me up probably 
destroyed Cyberse World.

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:30.700
That’s…

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:33.670
It’s you.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:37.670
What are you trying to do?

00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:39.410
A test.

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:44.880
This is a new card to protect 
Cyberse World from humans.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:49.210
It seems pointless to hide it.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.220
I sense something disturbing about you.

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:57.220
I knew you’re the one I 
should be worried about.

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:04.960
What are you doing?

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:08.030
What's the point of doing this?

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:17.860
In order to further my plans, 
I'll first erase Cyberse World.

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:20.220
I won’t let you interfere.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:29.850
I can’t forgive him for doing that to you!

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.460
Earth…

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:36.160
We’re being chased.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:38.320
He already found us?

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:41.530
What I'm sensing isn't the Light Ignis.

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:51.770
That's…

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:54.440
Earth appeared!

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:57.250
I’m sending you the 
location!  Go immediately!

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:01.960
It’s too far from here.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.570
We’ll go!

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:15.400
No good!  We can’t escape him!

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:19.510
Aqua, I’m sorry.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:22.710
Earth!

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:25.720
Aqua, flee.

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.020
What?

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:34.750
Stop!

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:36.720
I’m your opponent!

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:40.110
I thought I'd deal with 
the easy one first, but…

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:42.700
Fine.  Let’s duel.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:47.060
There!  It’s Earth!

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.860
Earth!

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:51.460
Ai?

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:52.830
Playmaker.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.000
Who are you?

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.940
I’m SOL’s bounty hunter.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:00.910
That voice…  Can it be?

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.360
Oh my!

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:08.750
I already challenged him to a duel.

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:12.590
Playmaker, I'll deal with you after him.

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:17.070
I won’t let you lay a hand on Aqua!

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:19.110
Speed Duel!

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.500
They started their duel!

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:30.080
But why has Onizuka lost so much weight?

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:32.670
What worries me more is…

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:34.910
You sense it too?

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:37.540
Something unfamiliar…

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:41.380
I’ll go first, Ignis.

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:51.520
Why is Go Onizuka there?

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:54.230
He hasn't fully recovered yet.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:58.200
Direct orders from higher up.

00:11:58.580 --> 00:12:00.670
The Queen.

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:03.680
Akira is sending video.

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:07.890
It's the Ignis and… Go Onizuka?

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:09.600
My turn!

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:11.740
I set a monster.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:14.220
I end my turn.

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:16.720
He only set a card?

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:20.690
It’s not just his appearance.  
He also changed his playstyle.

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:25.660
What happened to Go Onizuka?

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:26.840
Here I go.

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:29.800
My turn!  I draw!

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:33.640
From my hand, I activate 
the spell card, Cost Down.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:38.400
I discard a card to lower Rock 
Hammer’s Level by 2 and summon it!

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:42.480
Rock Hammer’s effect!

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:49.850
By tributing this card, I Special Summon 
three G Golem Tokens in defense position!

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:54.090
Appear!  The circuit that roars the land!

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:57.590
Link Summon!

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:02.400
Appear, Link 2 G Golem Stubborn Menhir!

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:05.160
Appear again!

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:06.980
The circuit that roars the land!

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:10.710
The summoning conditions are two Cyberses!

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:12.940
Link Summon!

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:15.650
Appear, Link 2!

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:20.820
G Golem Crystal Heart!

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:25.760
He used Link 3 Materials, but 
he summoned a Link 2 monster?

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:29.300
It’s a special card he received from Aqua.

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:31.390
It's worth a Link 3.

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:35.200
G Golem Crystal Heart’s effect!

00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:42.670
I Special Summon an Earth Link Monster from 
my graveyard and co-link it with this monster!

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:46.530
Come out, G Golem Stubborn Menhir!

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:53.080
When this effect is used, I place one 
G Golem Counter on Crystal Heart.

00:13:53.340 --> 00:14:01.830
For every G Golem Counter, the Earth 
monster next to its link gains 600 ATK!

00:14:01.830 --> 00:14:04.800
Next, Stubborn Menhir’s effect!

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:12.030
I Special Summon a Normal Summon-capable Earth 
monster from my graveyard by negating its effects.

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:14.540
Come out, Rock Hammer!

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.740
I see.  I understand.

00:14:18.740 --> 00:14:23.710
It looks like a wasteful summoning method 
at first glance, but it's more efficient.

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:27.450
Appear!  The circuit that roars the land!

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:32.120
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Earth monsters!

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:38.270
I set Rock Hammer and Link 2 Stubborn 
Menhir in the Link Markers!

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:39.460
Link Summon!

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:46.210
Appear, Link 3 G Golem Invalid Dolmen!

00:14:48.140 --> 00:14:50.160
Crystal Heart’s effect!

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:55.540
It gains 600 ATK per G Golem Counter!

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:02.960
Nice!  His deck is better than 
when he battled Playmaker!

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:06.390
I set one card and battle!

00:15:06.390 --> 00:15:10.160
Invalid Dolmen attacks your monster!

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:17.040
The monster I set is Dinowrestler Capaptera!

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:21.940
Invalid Dolmen’s effect!

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:30.290
When this card attacks a monster in defense 
position, it deals piercing damage!

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:36.220
I send Dinowrestler Martial Ampelo from my 
hand to the graveyard to activate its effect.

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:40.070
When a Dinowrestler battles 
your monster that has

00:15:40.070 --> 00:15:43.320
equal or higher ATK, it’s 
not destroyed in battle.

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:46.800
And the battle damage I take is halved!

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:57.110
I end my turn.

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.490
Earth has the advantage.

00:15:59.490 --> 00:16:02.080
The Ignis are impressive.

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:06.320
Aoi?

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:08.940
I’m going to LINK VRAINS.

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:12.320
I can’t do anything from here.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:15.800
You stay and give me status updates.

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:17.520
O-Okay...

00:16:18.090 --> 00:16:23.270
Those Ignis may side with us, 
so I can’t let him have them.

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:25.580
Y-You’re right.

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:30.910
You’ve matured.

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:40.810
My turn.  I draw!

00:16:41.590 --> 00:16:43.820
Capaptera’s effect activates.

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:51.060
When you have more monsters than me, one 
monster on your field goes to the graveyard.

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:55.030
I send Invalid Dolmen to the graveyard.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:56.500
That’s pointless!

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:58.930
When I have Invalid Dolmen,

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:05.050
your monsters can't affect Crystal Heart 
and Invalid Dolmen when they're co-linked!

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:09.980
In that case, I Special Summon 
Dinowrestler Pankratops from my hand.

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:14.350
A Level 7 monster!

00:17:14.350 --> 00:17:20.560
When you have more monsters than 
me, I can Special Summon this card.

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:24.670
Next, I summon Dinowrestler Eskrimamenchi.

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:32.040
I can summon this card without tributing 
when there’s a Dinowrestler on the field.

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:36.270
Appear!  The circuit to victory!

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:42.020
I set Capaptera, Eskrimamenchi and 
Pankratops in the Link Markers.

00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:45.620
Link Summon!

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:52.960
Appear, Link 3 Dinowrestler King T Wrextle!

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:55.660
That’s Go Onizuka’s ace.

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:58.360
I activate Capaptera’s 
effect from my graveyard.

00:17:58.360 --> 00:18:03.090
When it's sent to the graveyard 
to Link Summon a Dinowrestler...

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:07.600
...that Dinowrestler gains 1000 
ATK until the end of turn.

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:11.560
Battle!

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:19.860
When King T Wrextle battles, you 
can’t activate spell or trap cards.

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:22.450
Rout Crystal Heart!

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:24.480
I won’t let you!

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:31.590
When Invalid Dolmen is in the Monster Zone...

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:36.570
...attacking monsters must attack this card!

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:40.040
I won’t let you lay a 
finger on Crystal Heart!

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:44.440
All right!  He stopped Crystal 
Heart’s destruction!

00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:45.510
However…

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:54.460
King T Wrextle has 4000 ATK.

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:57.650
Invalid Dolmen can’t stop it.

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:06.230
But Invalid Dolmen’s effect now activates!

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:13.970
When it's destroyed, the effects of all 
faceup cards on your field are negated!

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:18.440
All right!  He removed 
King T Wrextle’s effect!

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:21.910
Then I activate the trap 
card, Gravity Vision!

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:29.510
It activates by targeting an Earth Link 
Monster destroyed in battle and your monster.

00:19:29.510 --> 00:19:33.690
I Special Summon a G Golem 
Token in defense position.

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:41.200
It gains 800 DEF for every Link Marker 
that the destroyed Earth Link Monster had.

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:44.410
Invalid Dolmen has three Link Markers!

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:47.410
Therefore, it has 2400 DEF!

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:49.990
And as long as I have the

00:19:49.990 --> 00:19:56.570
G Golem Token summoned using 
this effect, King T Wrextle loses ATK equal to its DEF!

00:19:56.910 --> 00:20:00.670
And it can’t attack a non-Token monster!

00:20:01.580 --> 00:20:03.730
Earth is impressive!

00:20:03.730 --> 00:20:07.590
Now King T Wrextle can’t 
get past that Token!

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:11.270
It’s true that Earth’s 
defense is strong, but…

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:14.260
Why is Go Onizuka so confident?

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:16.770
You're quite skilled.

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:20.730
Then I'll show you my new power.

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:24.710
Expanding thought capabilities!  Brain Hack!

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:30.410
What?

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:35.620
What did he do?

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:41.960
I activate Dinowrestler Eskrimamenchi’s 
effect from my graveyard!

00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:46.620
When a monster is Special Summoned 
to your field during my turn,

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:48.980
I return this card to my hand.

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:54.940
And I Special Summon a Level 4 or 
lower Dinowrestler from my graveyard!

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:58.570
I Special Summon Dinowrestler Capaptera.

